    "result_text": "All green. The full test suite (the one runnable test class, `AcceptanceTest`, plus its abstract base and helper) passes, including the new `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` checkpoint.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `customerCode` is a derived, server-assigned field, so I mirrored the existing pattern used for `registrationDate` (a dedicated single-responsibility component invoked from the create endpoint) rather than piling logic into the controller.\n\n**New component** \u2014 `rest/controller/CustomerCodeAssigner.java`, parallel to `RegistrationDateDefaulter`:\n- Builds the code as `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", prefix, sequence)` where `prefix` is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `sequence = countOwners() + 1`.\n- Called in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` *before* `saveOwner`, so the sequence reflects owners already stored.\n\n**Owner count** threaded cleanly through the existing layers:\n- `OwnerRepository.count()` \u2014 implemented in the JPA (`COUNT` query) and JDBC (`SELECT COUNT(*)`) impls; the Spring Data JPA repo (the active profile) inherits it from the base repository.\n- `ClinicService.countOwners()` \u2192 `ownerRepository.count()`.\n\n**Persistence & serialization**:\n- `Owner` entity: `customer_code` column with getter/setter, added to `toString`.\n- `openapi.yml`: `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema \u2014 so MapStruct maps it onto `OwnerDto` automatically (same mechanism as `displayName`/`initials`), and it appears in `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n- `customer_code` column added to all four DB schemas (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) at the end of the table so the column-explicit seed inserts are unaffected.\n\nThe test creates `smithers` then `jones` against 10 seed owners, yielding `SMI-0011` and `JON-0012` \u2014 start-prefixes and the +1 global sequence both hold.",
